## Rules

<!-- Between 3 and 7 rules, every one specific to this project. Generic advice
     ("write clean code") does not belong in layer 0. The first three slots are
     mandatory: where output is written, what must never be edited, and the
     evidence standard. Fill the rest with what actually bites people here. -->

1. Compiled output is written to `{{OUTPUT_PATH}}`. Nothing else writes there, and nothing there is hand-edited without also fixing the source it came from.
2. Never edit `raw/`. It is the evidence. A correction goes in the article that cites the raw file, never in the raw file itself.
3. Every load-bearing fact in `{{WIKI_PATH}}`, meaning every number, date and quote, appears verbatim in a `raw/` file that the article names in its Raw line.
